Package: mzimp
Title: Zero-Inflated Mixed Poisson Regression for Multivariate Count
        Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Quang Huy",
        family = "Nguyen",
        email = "huynqtkt@neu.edu.vn",
        role = c("aut", "cre",  "cph")
    )
Description: Fits and selects zero-inflated mixed Poisson models for
    multivariate count regression. Supports multiple mixing distributions
    and variance specifications for flexible marginal modeling, while
    allowing dependence in the structural-zero components and latent
    mixing intensities to be modeled separately through copulas.
    The methodology is described in Nguyen (2026)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2608.12732>.
